---
/* ============================================================
   Bearings — /sessions (the depth track)

   Deliberately its own entry point rather than woven into /before
   or /integration. Most people opening this app want one card and
   an early night; this page is for the much smaller case of
   someone doing repeated, deliberate, solo work and wanting a
   record across occasions. Keeping it separate means the default
   path never acquires the weight of a program, and nobody has to
   opt out of something they did not ask for.

   Not linked from the shelves for the same reason. It is in the
   nav, findable, and otherwise quiet.
   ============================================================ */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SessionTracker from "../components/SessionTracker.svelte";
import CoolingLedger from "../components/CoolingLedger.svelte";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sessions — Bearings"
  description="An optional record across occasions: a question held beforehand, what you wrote after, and decisions you want to look at again."
  section="sessions"
>
  <section class="reading">
    <p class="kicker">On this device only</p>
    <h1>Sessions</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      For repeated, deliberate work. This page keeps a plain record across
      occasions — a question you chose to hold, what you wrote in the days
      after, and any decision you want to reread later.
    </p>
    <p>
      It never interprets any of it. There is no progress here, nothing to
      complete, and no version of using this page correctly. If you came for a
      single experience and have no interest in tracking anything, the rest of
      Bearings works without this page and you can ignore it entirely.
    </p>
    <p class="detail">
      Everything below is stored unencrypted in this browser, like the rest of
      your notes. Anyone with access to this device and an unlocked browser can
      read it. Settings has a copy-out and a delete-everything.
    </p>
  </section>

  <SessionTracker client:load />
  <CoolingLedger client:load />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  section {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }
  .detail {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    padding-left: var(--space-3);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--rule);
  }
</style>
